    "updated_at": "2026-11-07T22:22:32Z",
    "body": "PR #162 (stacked on nothing; `feat`, merges at the next cut): a Tormach PathPilot post and a Tormach 770MX machine (inch), and `machine.units` so an inch machine file posts G20 programs. It says `Refs #131`, so this issue stays open for the hardware results and the MicroArc 4th axis.\n\nChecked against two PathPilot 2.12 Conversational facing programs (defaults, inch): same framing (no %, no O word), G30 before T.. M6 then G43 H.., and the same ending (Z up, G30, M30). Deliberate difference: G64 P0.001, tighter than Conversational's P0.005 Q0.\n\nNext: posted samples (face, contour, pocket, peck drill, tap) go through PathPilot Hub v2.14.4 first; then a dry run, an air cut and a soft-material cut on the 770MX. Results will be reported here.",
    "author_association": "COLLABORATOR",
