    "body": "Hardware results for PR #162 (posted samples, inch), on the contributor's Tormach 770MX with PathPilot 2.14.4, as air cuts:\n- 01-face, 02-contour, 03-pocket, 04-peck-drill: run to the end, including real ATC tool changes (Z up, G30, T.. M6, G43 H..) with X/Y positioned before Z comes down, and the G73 peck.\n- 05-tap (G84, 600 rpm, F15 = rpm × 0.025 in pitch, high belt): runs clean. Rigid tapping works as posted. The PathPilot Hub simulator stops every rigid tap with a constant ~9-turn overshoot; that's a simulator limit, not the post.\n- 05b-tap-300rpm: PathPilot refused S300 in the high range, then timed out reaching speed when the range setting didn't match the belt's pulley position. That's operator setup, and it's what the post's \"NEEDS THE LOW BELT RANGE\" comment flags.\n- \"Program exceeds machine maximum\" warnings in Hub and on the machine came from where G54 and the tool length sat, and cleared when G54 was moved.\n\nStill open under #131: a cut in material, and the MicroArc 4th axis. Machine files for other Tormach mills: #170.",
    "author_association": "COLLABORATOR",
