    "body": "First real CamCraft job run on the 770MX (PathPilot 2.14.4): Face + 2D Contour from the GUI, posted with the Tormach PathPilot post, G54 Z0 on the stock top, tool T31 with its length from the tool setter. It ran correctly after two hand edits to the posted file:\n1. T1/H1 → T31/H31. CamCraft numbers tools by list position; filed as #221. Note: the unedited file ran with H1, applied tool 1's length, and stopped ~1.5 in high. It failed safe this time, but a shorter H1 would have cut too deep. #221 matters.\n2. A `G0 Z0.9843` before the face's first feed. The program otherwise fed from the top of Z travel at the plunge rate. Now done by the post (PR #162, latest commit), pinned by tormach_post::a_face_job_on_the_built_in_770mx_passes_the_gate_and_posts_inch.",
